 "title": "Welcome to Kanabec County, MN",
 "text": "Welcome to Kanabec County, MN\nSKIP TO CONTENT\nHome\nDEPARTMENTS\nBOARD INFORMATION\nAGENDAS & MINUTES\nCOUNTY ORDINANCES\nPUBLIC NOTICE\nCOMMITTEES, BOARDS & COMMISSIONS\nCOORDINATOR\nCAREER OPPORTUNITIES\nUNION LABOR CONTRACTS\nEMPLOYEE LINKS\nASSESSOR\nATTORNEY\nAUDITOR\\TREASURER\nKANABEC COUNTY DISTRICT COURT\nKANABEC COUNTY EDA\nEMERGENCY MANAGEMENT\nFAMILY SERVICES\nPUBLIC WORKS\nHIGHWAY\nENVIRONMENTAL SERVICES\nSURVEYOR\nGIS\nPROBATION\nPUBLIC HEALTH\nRECORDER\nBirth or Death Certificates\nMarriage Licenses\nRecording Services\nMilitary Discharge Records\nNotary Public\nMinister Credentials\nFrequently Asked Questions\nInteractive GIS Mapping\nSHERIFF\nTRANSIT\nVETERANS SERVICES\nCOMMUNITY\nDRIVERS LICENSE\nKANABEC SOIL & WATER\nSNAKE RIVER WATERSHED\nZONING INFORMATION\nTOWNSHIP & CITY INFORMATION\nKNIFE LAKE IMPROVEMENT DISTRICT\nU of M EXTENSION\nMORA CHAMBER\nPLANNING COMMISSION\nBOARD OF ADJUSTMENT\nBETTER TOGETHER COALITION\nMNDOT HWY 65/23 MORA CORRIDOR STUDY\nHIGHWAY 65 COALITION\nFINGERPRINTING SERVICES\nEAST CENTRAL REGIONAL LIBRARY\nAFFORDABLE HOUSING OPPORTUNITIES\nABOUT US\nHOW DO I...\nSearch\nPrev Next\nPROPERTY TAX STATEMENTS & PAYMENTS\nHome DEPARTMENTS AUDITOR\\TREASURER PROPERTY TAX STATEMENTS & PAYMENTS\nSub Menu\nPROPERTY TAX INFORMATION\nPROPERTY TAX STATEMENTS & PAYMENTS\nELECTIONS\nCURRENT STATE & COUNTY OFFICIALS\nCURRENT CITY & TOWNSHIP OFFICIALS\nFAQ - ELECTIONS\nLICENSES & PERMITS\nRegulated Gatherings\nTobacco License\nLiquor License\nAuctioneer License\nFireworks Permit\nPrecious Metal License\nPASSPORTS\nFEE SCHEDULE\nTAX FORFEIT LAND SALE\nAPPLICATIONS/FORMS\nFINANCE\n|\n*2026 Property Tax Statements were mailed March 20, 2026.\nTo download a copy of your 2026 Property Tax Statement, click here *\nStatements\nTax statements for real estate and personal property are mailed once a year, by the end of March. Statements for manufactured homes are mailed in July. No second notice is sent. Failure to receive a property tax statement does not exempt the taxpayer from timely payment of taxes due .\nRequest to change Property Tax mailing address form\nPayment Due Dates\nDue Dates |\nType of Tax/Classification |\nMay 15 - first half |\nResidential and agricultural classifications excludes mobile homes |\nMay 15 |\nTaxes due in full if amount is $50 or less |\nAugust 31 - first half |\nManufactured homes |\nAugust 31 |\nManufactured home taxes due in full if amount is $50 or less |\nOctober 15 - second half |\nResidential classification only |\nNovember 15 - second half |\nManufactured home and agricultural classifications |\nIf the 15th falls on a Saturday, Sunday or legal holiday, the due date is the next regular business day. Taxes become past due after the due date.\nAs of January 1st, of the year following the due date, taxes become delinquent. Example, 2025 taxes not paid during the calendar year of 2025 became delinquent on January 1, 2026.\nPenalty will vary depending on classification and the date they are paid. The schedule is on the back of the tax statement or click here .\nPayment Options\nPaying by Credit Card or E-Check - click here\nCredit Card Processing Fee (convenience fee) is charged by Autoagent. Credit or Debit cards are charged 2.65 % of the amount of the customer's payment. There is a minimum fee of $2.00. E-Checks - $1.50 per transaction.\nBy phone: 1-320-433-7717 - Credit Card or E-Check\nThis is an automated phone line. Please have the property ID number and amount due before making a payment. Credit Card Processing Fee (convenience fee) is charged by Autoagent. Credit or Debit cards are charge 2.65 % of the amount of the customer's payment. There is a minimum fee of $2.00. E-Checks - $1.50 per transaction.\nIn Person:\n8:00 am to 4:30 pm, Monday through Friday at the Kanabec County Courthouse, Auditor-Treasurer's office, 2nd floor. Please bring your property tax stubs and have payment ready to service you faster.\nBy Mail:\nMail payments to: Kanabec County Auditor-Treasurer, 317 Maple Ave E, Ste 261A, Mora, MN 55051\nDrop Box:\nThere is a drop box located to the left of the front door at Kanabec County Courthouse, 317 Maple Ave E, Mora, MN 55051\nEscrow:\nYour lending institution may be escrowing your taxes for you. If you have questions regarding your escrow, contact your mortgage company or lending institution.\nNSF Policy\nAll checks or electronic payments returned to Kanabec County for non-sufficient funds (NSF) will be charged a $30.00 NSF fee. Unpaid NSF fees will be assessed on to the next tax year.\nPlease note: Online and phone payments may take a few days to show as paid.\n© 2016 Kanabec County | Web Accessibility Policy 317 Maple Avenue East Mora, MN 55051\nCoordinator's Office: 320-679-6440\nPowered By Revize\nLogin",
